KAE - Kunpeng Accelerator Engine
Upstream source: https://gitcode.com/boostkit/KAE

Original KAE contributions include:
Copyright (c) 2026 Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.
Copyright 2020-2021 Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd. (UADK)
Copyright (c) 2019 HiSilicon Limited. (kernel queue manager)
Individual files retain their dates, authors and third-party attributions.

KAE user-space contributions, UADK and this Debian packaging use Apache-2.0.
The full Apache-2.0 text is in /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0.
Kernel drivers retain GPL-2.0-only or GPL-2.0-or-later, as specified by each
source file; UAPI headers additionally retain the Linux-syscall-note exception.
The full GPL version 2 text is in /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2.

The bundled zlib is Copyright Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler and uses the
zlib license. Zstandard is Copyright Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates;
KAE selects its BSD-3-Clause option as recorded in LICENSE.zstd. LZ4 libraries
are Copyright Yann Collet and use BSD-2-Clause; its command-line code retains
GPL-2.0-or-later. The upstream KAELz4 notice selects GPLv3 when combining that
command-line code with the Apache-2.0 KAE contributions. Snappy is Copyright
Google Inc. and uses BSD-3-Clause, with additional test-data exceptions noted
in its upstream inventory. gzip retains its Free Software Foundation and
individual contributor notices and GPL-3.0-or-later terms. The full GPL version
3 text is in /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3.

Legacy OpenSSL-derived and GmSSL-derived source portions retain their original
licenses and attributions. The file-specific scope, full license texts and
upstream acknowledgements are reproduced unchanged in the following files
under this package's /usr/share/doc directory:

 licenses/KAEOpensslEngine-LICENSE.openssl
 licenses/KAEOpensslEngine-LICENSE.gmssl
 licenses/KAEZlib-LICENSE.zlib
 licenses/KAEZstd-LICENSE.zstd
 licenses/KAELz4-LICENSE.lz4
 licenses/KAESnappy-LICENSE.snappy

The source package also preserves all per-file notices, component LICENSE
files, and the upstream source archives and their license inventories.
